{"groups":[{"members":["c1"],"primary":"c1","title":"Newly Constructed Multiple Dwellings Law: 30-year exemption from local rent control","requirement":"Newly constructed multiple dwellings are exempt from any local rent control or rent leveling ordinance for 30 years after construction is completed. New Jersey has no statewide rent cap, and municipalities may adopt their own rent control ordinances.","key_value":"30-year exemption from local rent control after completion of construction","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:42-84.5","coverage_conditions":"Applies to newly constructed multiple dwellings for 30 years following completion of construction. During that period they are exempt from municipal rent control ordinances.","exemptions":"Separately, these are also not subject to municipal rent control: rents subsidized by governmental funding, HUD-owned or HUD-subsidized housing, HUD-insured developments that HUD determines have certain economic problems, and NJHMFA-financed projects whose rents the NJHMFA fixes and controls.","coverage_from":"c1","conflict_note":null},{"members":["c2"],"primary":"c2","title":"Anti-Eviction Act: rent increases must not be unconscionable","requirement":"A landlord may not raise rent mid-lease and must end the old lease with written notice that the tenant may stay at the increased rent. Any increase must not be unconscionable, must comply with any municipal rent ordinance, and may not recover costs that result solely from conversion to a condominium, cooperative or fee simple ownership.","key_value":"No numeric cap; increase must not be unconscionable","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1 et seq.; N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.31","coverage_conditions":"Applies to residential tenancies covered by the Anti-Eviction Act. Before evicting for nonpayment of an increased rent, the landlord must serve a valid notice to quit and a notice of rent increase.","exemptions":"Rent may be increased for new services or amenities, even in connection with a conversion.","coverage_from":"c2","conflict_note":null}],"dropped":[]}
